# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# `.dockerignore` governs what enters the *image*; this governs what leaves your
# *machine*. Both matter, and they are not the same thing: without this file
# gcloud falls back to `.gitignore`, which today happens to exclude the same
# patterns — but nothing keeps the two lists in step, and the next person to add
# a secret pattern to `.dockerignore` would silently upload it.
#
# Keep the secret patterns here identical to `.dockerignore`.
#
# Nothing listed below is needed by the build: the image builds the web app from
# `web/` sources, resolves the API from `api/pyproject.toml` + `api/uv.lock`, and
# copies only `docs/openapi.json`, `docs/examples/` and `data/activities.json`.

# --- secrets: never uploaded, let alone built -------------------------------
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
service-account*.json
gcloud-service-account*.json

# --- git and CI --------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude

# --- dependency trees and build output (the image builds its own) ------------
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/.vite
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.cache
api/htmlcov
.coverage
coverage

# --- local environment and editor noise --------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
.idea
.vscode

# --- test suites: CI runs these against the source, never inside the image ---
api/tests
web/src/**/*.test.ts
web/src/**/*.test.tsx